### ⏱️ 3. Static Timing Analysis (STA)
* [cite_start]**Timing Constraints:** Define Setup and Hold times, their equations, and explain how to fix violations[cite: 178].
* [cite_start]**Clock Degradation Metrics:** Analyze the effect of Clock Skew, Jitter, and Propagation Delay on the maximum clock frequency ($F_{max}$)[cite: 179].
* [cite_start]**Circuit Timing Problem:** * *Problem Statement:* Consider the circuit diagram and the timing requirement as shown for the flip flop[cite: 180]. [cite_start]Two clock buffers are added at the clock pin and the output pin[cite: 181]. [cite_start]Also a combinational delay of $dly = 0.2\text{ns}$ is present in the input to the output path[cite: 182].
    
    ![STA Circuit Diagram](uploaded:image_742465.png-8799fdd6-9bfd-4521-a2d7-32b51f0c8679)
    
    * [cite_start]*Parameters:* * $T_{cq} = 1.5\text{ns}$ [cite: 186]
        * [cite_start]$T_{su} = 1\text{ns}$ [cite: 186]
        * [cite_start]$T_{h} = 2\text{ns}$ [cite: 186]
        * [cite_start]Initial $dly = 0.2\text{ns}$ [cite: 182, 185]
    * [cite_start]*Question:* Check for any violation in the circuit with the given timing requirements, and if there is any violation then what would be the updated value of $dly$[cite: 188]? [cite_start]Also is there any effect on $f_{maximum}$ due to added clock buffers[cite: 189]?

#### 💡 Solution:
1. [cite_start]**Hold Violation Verification:** $$T_{hold} \le T_{clock\_Q} + dly$$ [cite: 193]
   [cite_start]$$2\text{ns} \le 1.5\text{ns} + 0.2\text{ns}$$ [cite: 194]
   [cite_start]$$2\text{ns} \le 1.7\text{ns} \quad \mathbf{[FAIL]}$$ [cite: 195]
   [cite_start]Since the condition fails, there is a **hold time violation** in the circuit[cite: 195].
2. [cite_start]**Remediation & Correction:** To remove the hold violation, we must vary $dly$[cite: 196]:
   [cite_start]$$dly \ge T_{hold} - T_{clock\_Q}$$ [cite: 198]
   [cite_start]$$dly \ge 2\text{ns} - 1.5\text{ns}$$ [cite: 199]
   [cite_start]$$dly \ge 0.5\text{ns}$$ [cite: 200]
   [cite_start]The $dly$ parameter must be greater than or equal to **$0.5\text{ns}$** to completely avoid a hold violation in this circuit[cite: 200].
3. [cite_start]**Buffer Frequency Impact:** The added clock buffer delays **do not affect** the $f_{maximum}$ of this path circuit[cite: 201].

